, prioritizing existing exports\/reference metadata; exact counts only at prequalified resource-isolated targets; no viable path=>clear fallback\/deferral.\nRead existing docs\/table-count-guideline.md, table-count-calibration.md, sqlserver-table-count-guideline.md and results\/reviews\/final-all-proof.json, results\/sqlserver\/owner-proof.json plus underlying relevant JSON and old final acceptance. Use Python to parse allowlisted fields, not giant raw dumps. Existing source and validated mechanisms remain authoritative. Existing MySQL\/SQL Server final docs are frozen evidence\/detail; new files are the FINAL user-facing selection playbooks. docs\/README.md is Japanese index linking both new files first, then old evidence\/reproduction details. Do not edit rootREADME (bound by old acceptance).\nEach product playbook should be practical ~120-170lines: quick conclusion\/algorithm, precision\/freshness choice table, comprehensive table-state decision matrix, bounded usable SQL snippets, operator start\/stop\/end\/recovery checklist, short observed precision\/cost limits with relative links to immutable evidence\/detail. Avoid engine encyclopedia or long workflow implementation chatter. All observed numbers must derive from resultsJSON. No new made-up data or numeric production safety values. If timeout examples use literal budgets, label examples and require owner budgets and driver deadlines BEFORE copy\/paste. Per-table\/shard result record including UNKNOWN and incomplete totals. New final acceptance record will be results\/reviews\/final-guidelines\/acceptance.json; do not claim completed reviews yet. No doc change after final2role reviews without re-review.\nShared route\/state coverage (combine physical, activity, security and acquisition axes; acknowledge combinations and unknown states, not just one huge synthetic grid): known\/unknown\/0\/NULL\/missing\/denied metadata; empty\/tiny\/huge; rowwidth80\/100\/LOB\/row overflow; PK exists\/absent\/string\/sparse\/skew; no secondary\/narrow secondary\/multiple\/invisible\/filtered indexes as applicable; partition whole-object vs partition rows; compression\/cache warm\/cold\/stale or uninitialized stats; heavy updates\/INSERT\/DELETE\/soft-delete and long open transactions; concurrent DDL\/rebuild\/migration\/truncate\/object generation; TDE\/serverkeys available or unavailable vs application ciphertext\/client seed unknown; privileges\/RLS\/tenant scope; primary\/dedicated\/shared replica\/independent restored copy\/none, freshness; logical views vs physical tables, temporary\/session-local, nonstandard engine\/storage, external\/remote\/synonyms, temporalcurrent\/history, shards\/missing targets. Not every axis needs a unique SQL; make SAME normal safe path cover most ordinary variants. Explain unsupported\/out-of-scope precise fallback, reference source, or what owner must supply; no error =>0 or blind primary scan.\nMySQL: normal InnoDB BASE TABLE across row\/index\/partition\/compression\/ciphertext\/gap\/PK variants uses same approved export\/I_S.TABLES.TABLE_ROWS reference and qualified isolated ordinary SELECT COUNT(*), new dedicated non-enlisted non-pooled session RC\/RR\/autocommit1 initialized before tables. Table metadata scoped by DB\/name and engine\/type; no expensive discovery scan. row_count0 not confirmed empty. Stats expiry nonzero still cache miss\/expiry engine reads, existing0 not silently overwritten; no autoANALYZE\/index creation\/cacheflush or EXPLAIN ANALYZE. OrdinarySELECT RC\/RR row-nonlocking but MDL\/undo\/resources remain; embedded DML\/CTAS\/SET count, locking reads\/SERIALIZABLE\/global\/table locks excluded. No COUNT(nullablecol) or PKrangeID surrogate. NonInnoDB\/MyISAM\/MEMORY\/temporary\/views: do not automatically use InnoDB count assumptions; inventory\/reference from approved source, owner-specific isolated or export route, no production locking count. TABLES metadata omits some temporary\/session objects; missing never0. Metadata TABLES whole logical table avoids summing TABLES plus PARTITIONS or duplicates. For exact whole partitioned table COUNT whole table with qualified snapshot, not changing partitions+sum. SQLvisible intPK permits conditional sample prototype only after all provedeligibility; not default and never infer empty\/smallness from uncertifiedsample0. Logical restore stats cannot calibrate old productioncache error without matching profile\/generation\/time. TDE requires SERVER keys even if SQLclient has no seed; backuprestore requireskeyprovision. Initial roughsmallness never productionCOUNT permission. Unknown PK\/rowwidth is not reason to abandon ordinaryCOUNT at qualified target.\nSQL Server: partition DMV SUM(row_count) index_id IN(0,1), sum all partitions, avoid NCI doublecount; fallback sys.partitions for suitably visible approved scope, reference not exact; permission2022+ VIEW DATABASE PERFORMANCE STATE +VIEW SECURITY DEFINITION, do not autoGRANT. Optimizer sys.dm_db_stats_properties rows update-time (filteredstats distinct), not currentpartitioncounter; no automaticUPDATESTATS. Initial table\/identity\/context guard, reference0 not certified empty. Normal disk-based heap\/clustered\/partitioned\/compressed\/wide\/ciphertext physical tables (and supported diskcolumnstore) keep standard metadata and qualifiedCOUNT_BIG paths, not blanket-defer due lack of every state measurement; columnstore delta\/deletes make metadata approximate, no performance\/ranking promise from onlyOPENdelta fixture. For specialmemoryoptimized\/external\/remote\/synonym\/temp\/temporal\/view clearly identify count meaning, permissions and owner-approved route instead of blindlyrunninggenericSQL. Temporal current\/history are distinct objects and semantics; no automaticuniondoublecount. RLS COUNT visible context differs from wholephysicalmetadata; globalmetadata nevertenant exact. COUNT_BIG avoidsint overflow, star countsNULL rows. ExistingRCSI READCOMMITTED or existingallowedSNAPSHOT only; defaultlockingRC not safe nonlocking path. Do not auto enableproductionRCSI or useNOLOCK\/READPAST\/TABLOCK\/SERIALIZABLE. Require new noambient dedicated session, existingtransaction rejection via @@TRANCOUNT\/XACT_STATE, SETIMPLICIT_TRANSACTIONS OFF before metadata\/count, SNAPSHOT shortexplicittransaction and confirmedzero\/end. SETLOCK_TIMEOUT is NOT commandtimeout; driverdeadline+separate cancelowner verifies ownedcurrentSPID\/context\/login\/start, no blindKILLreusedID, rollback\/serverend and recovery before nexttable. SchS\/SchM, versionstore\/tempdb\/PVS\/longtransactions and CPU\/IO remain. AG readable secondary maps diskreads to snapshot but even separatehardware can affectPRIMARY ghostcleanup\/space\/logreuse; existing approved primary+secondary monitoring, data\/logcapacity, data movement\/disconnect, stop\/recovery budgets required, or independent approved restoredcopy\/defer. Replica\/backup provisioning themselves budgeted. App ciphertext vs actualAlwaysEncrypted driver unmeasured; no clientkeybypass promise whenservercan'tread.\nUse official primary source links for new technical claims; web browsing allowed, primarydocs only. Prior accepted guidelines contain official links. Observation sets\/hardware\/support boundary explicit (SQL emulated ARMamd64 unsupported, not nativeperformance; both lack100M80\/100wideTDEcombo). Use few concise useful observed error examples (MySQL metadata can exceed10%; SQLDMV27positiveobservationsmatched but not bound; optimizerstale rows differentmechanism) or link precision table rather than clutter many timings. Don't make every engineer run lab\/Riela to use guideline; final review acceptance is audit appendix, not production prerequisite. Capture acquisition identities\/timestamps\/snapshotGTIDorLSN\/freshness\/precisionkind\/unknownreason\/budget\/end status\/missing shards; no global current exact claim across separate snapshots.\nReturn SMALL structured output: status, files, hashes, unresolvedMaterialIssues. No test mir